  "pipeline": {
    "source": "Packed editable high and low Blender sources; each physical surface and the shader receiver is accessible by name.",
    "bake": "Linux x86-64 Cycles CPU. Fixed triangulation, UV0 and corner normals on the matched receiver. One continuously connected ring is the projection pair; the removable field is excluded. Unlit EMIT for base color, roughness/metallic and emissive, tangent NORMAL and assembled 12-ray contact AO. Seam-normal corrections use the matched physical receiver finish in all channels.",
    "compression": "KTX-Software 4.4.2, 1024 square, 11 mips, UASTC/Zstandard; sRGB color/emission and linear tangent normal/ORM. All five encoded maps and PNG fallbacks are embedded in the GLB.",
    "determinism": "Two fresh generations matched byte-for-byte on all source PNGs, geometry report, glTF and vertex/index binary. Independent re-encoding and packaging matched all KTX2 files, GLB, model manifest and re-import report. Blend hashes identify the retained archives.",
    "review": "Apple M4 EEVEE, 24 samples at 768 square. Six matched camera pairs. Low reviews use the re-imported GLB with all five KTX2 maps decoded to level zero. Camera transforms and sources are recorded per view."
  },
