  "export_notice": "Blender reported multiple image nodes reaching one texture sampler. The exported document contains one sampler for all five textures, linear magnification and trilinear minification; the exact shared ORM, PNG and KTX2 bindings passed independent validation.",
  "corrections": [
    "First studio review exposed overly bright titanium, narrow side inserts, and a regular vortex pattern. The retained candidate has pearl tint, reduced micro-normal strength, widened dark blue inset panels with tapered ends, and a domain-warped multiscale vortex.",
    "Replaced the review-only solid wall lining with the cut host interface plane after close inspection showed the original calibration panel intersected the aperture throat.",
    "The glTF importer uses quaternion mode. The pose verifier now explicitly applies XYZ rotations and checks independently calculated wall, ceiling and oblique forward normals and the full shader offset vector."
  ],
